  "note": "Paired clean native release builds: develop@d55ab04388 (base) and the 0.4 Linux integration at d0c1891829 (candidate), which writes a background subagent run's settlement as a `bake.subagent.settled` Pi custom entry, durable before its notice is posted, beside scope 03, 04, 05, 11, 13, and 16 and D18 work that reaches no model request. Both arms set `subagents: true` and persistent sessions; the delegation scenario ran on all eight standard and extended model routes, three trials per arm, through the opn24 gateway (EVAL_GATEWAY): 48 samples, all successful. A delegation sample's usage is incomplete, because a child's requests pass the proxy but not the parent's event stream, so the table compares failures only (0 to 0 on every model); over all samples the base made 143 requests with 3 tool errors and the candidate 147 with 1. All 48 system prompts are identical once the arm's own executable path (named twice) and the workspace path are normalized, and tool-schema sizes match on every model; the candidate's 42 more first-request bytes are its longer checkout path. Most delegations were foreground calls, whose path is unchanged: 21 of 24 base and 23 of 24 candidate samples. Four were background runs, three base and one candidate; the candidate one, kimi-k2.7-code trial 2, wrote its settlement entry before its notice, and the model then received the same finished-notice text the base posts. Its one tool error was a `job_output` call with the subagent's id, which the existing error answers. The model-visible difference the change makes, a recorded settlement reported as finished rather than interrupted when the parent stops between recording and delivering it, needs a host stop, so the Rust restart and barrier tests cover it, not this run. No prompt, tool-definition, or fixture file under rust/ differs from develop, so the standard suite was not rerun, as for the 2026-10-18 subagents record. Raw samples remain in ignored .preflight/.",
